{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-4feb40e0-6715-43b7-85e5-112bbb30c00d","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9014942cf6dd9ec9","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9018-ut3o0c25/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9018-E001.md","content":"# Per-project GPU-hour report computation and export API\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the backend reporting capability for GPU chargeback: computation of per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable time ranges, built on top of the per-project GPU-hour usage data delivered by the in-flight GPU usage metering strategy (RHAISTRAT-9990), plus CSV export and a stable API that finance tooling can retrieve reports through. It does not re-implement or alter the metering collection pipeline — it consumes its output.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Compute per-project GPU-hour consumption totals and time-bucketed reports over administrator-selectable time ranges, sourcing all usage data from the metering data delivered by the GPU usage metering strategy.\n- Expose the computed reports through a stable API suitable for finance tooling retrieval.\n- Provide CSV export of report results.\n- Define and document the report output contract (fields, time-range semantics) that the administrator-facing Dashboard views and finance integrations build against.\n- Isolate the consumption of the metering data schema (owned by the metering strategy, not yet final) in the input mapping, so report semantics are decoupled from the upstream schema.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given per-project GPU-hour metering data as delivered by the GPU usage metering work, when a report is requested for a selectable time range, then per-project GPU-hour consumption totals are returned that reconcile with the underlying metered usage for that range.\n- Report results are exportable as CSV and retrievable via the stable API by a finance-tooling client, with the API contract documented.\n- A change to the metering data schema delivered by the metering strategy is absorbed in the input mapping without redesigning the report computation or the report output contract (rework is limited to the metering-data input mapping).\n- Report computation is validated end-to-end against metered usage data for at least one selectable time range, demonstrating correct attribution of consumption to projects.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable time ranges, computed from the metering data — this epic delivers the computation half.\n- HLR-2 (P1, bundled): CSV export and stable API retrieval for finance tooling — bundled with the P0 computation because both are output modes of the same aggregation over the same metering data on the same service surface; splitting would duplicate the aggregation and add an artificial boundary between one API surface.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- The metering data schema finalizes only when the GPU usage metering strategy (RHAISTRAT-9990) lands; that external timing is outside this epic's control and may force rework in the input mapping. The schema-isolation acceptance criterion above confines that rework surface.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":34377,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f1e0659ebd03b82","agent_id":"af8a5c09fb64dfbd9","session_id":"9043ac75-7a00-4a8d-a271-1ae0d81512e8","uuid":"df12755e-25c0-43de-b49a-97e5f5a2c613","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:22:11.721Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9018 into epics"}
