{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-0414c38b-82d0-4637-9acd-23517e3393d0","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a84558f258c09c2c","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9018-ut3o0c25/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9018-E002.md","content":"# Administrator chargeback reporting views in the Dashboard\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the administrator-facing reporting experience in the Dashboard: per-project GPU-hour consumption reports viewable over selectable time ranges, and an admin view showing current-month consumption against each project's Kueue quota. It consumes the report computation and export capability delivered by the report computation and export API work; it adds no data collection or aggregation of its own.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Add an administrator-facing view of per-project GPU-hour consumption reports with selectable time ranges, reading computed report data from the report API.\n- Add an admin view showing current-month per-project consumption against each project's Kueue quota, sourcing quota information from the Kueue quota objects the Dashboard already reads through the Kubernetes API.\n- Present both capabilities within the existing Dashboard administrator surfaces, consistent with current Dashboard navigation and role handling for administrator-facing sections.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given computed per-project GPU-hour report data, when an administrator selects a time range, then the Dashboard shows per-project GPU-hour consumption for that range.\n- Given current-month consumption data and each project's Kueue quota, when an administrator opens the admin consumption view, then current-month consumption is displayed against each project's Kueue quota.\n- The reporting views are accessible to platform administrators through the existing Dashboard console without new private component APIs or data-plane ownership in the Dashboard.\n- Report data displayed in the views reconciles with the same report retrieved via the export API for the identical time range.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): administrators can view per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable time ranges — this epic delivers the administrator-facing view half.\n- HLR-3 (P1, bundled): Dashboard admin view showing current-month consumption against each project's Kueue quota — bundled with the P0 report view because it is another presentation in the same administrator view surface consuming the same report data; splitting would build the same admin view surface twice.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Quota semantics follow the platform's Kueue quota model (ClusterQueue/LocalQueue); no quota-side backend work is expected — the Dashboard reads quota through the Kubernetes API today.\n- The metering data schema risk carried by the report computation work propagates here only through the report API contract, which is defined within this strategy.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":35187,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f1e0659ebd03b82","agent_id":"af8a5c09fb64dfbd9","session_id":"9043ac75-7a00-4a8d-a271-1ae0d81512e8","uuid":"b9191ca8-9f4d-4324-8155-51350703a42c","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:22:20.553Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9018 into epics"}
