{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-933c1e990de5a8fd","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9018-E002\n3\ttitle: Administrator chargeback reporting views in the Dashboard\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9018\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9018-E001\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 0\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 0\n17\t  external_dependency: 0\n18\t  human_process_gates: 0\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 4\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Administrator chargeback reporting views in the Dashboard\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tThis epic delivers the administrator-facing reporting experience in the Dashboard: per-project GPU-hour consumption reports viewable over selectable time ranges, and an admin view showing current-month consumption against each project's Kueue quota. It consumes the report computation and export capability delivered by the report computation and export API work; it adds no data collection or aggregation of its own.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Add an administrator-facing view of per-project GPU-hour consumption reports with selectable time ranges, reading computed report data from the report API.\n39\t- Add an admin view showing current-month per-project consumption against each project's Kueue quota, sourcing quota information from the Kueue quota objects the Dashboard already reads through the Kubernetes API.\n40\t- Present both capabilities within the existing Dashboard administrator surfaces, consistent with current Dashboard navigation and role handling for administrator-facing sections.\n41\t\n42\t## Acceptance Criteria\n43\t\n44\t- Given computed per-project GPU-hour report data, when an administrator selects a time range, then the Dashboard shows per-project GPU-hour consumption for that range.\n45\t- Given current-month consumption data and each project's Kueue quota, when an administrator opens the admin consumption view, then current-month consumption is displayed against each project's Kueue quota.\n46\t- The reporting views are accessible to platform administrators through the existing Dashboard console without new private component APIs or data-plane ownership in the Dashboard.\n47\t- Report data displayed in the views reconciles with the same report retrieved via the export API for the identical time range.\n48\t\n49\t## HLR Traceability\n50\t\n51\t- HLR-1 (P0): administrators can view per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable time ranges — this epic delivers the administrator-facing view half.\n52\t- HLR-3 (P1, bundled): Dashboard admin view showing current-month consumption against each project's Kueue quota — bundled with the P0 report view because it is another presentation in the same administrator view surface consuming the same report data; splitting would build the same admin view surface twice.\n53\t\n54\t## Risks / Notes\n55\t\n56\t- Quota semantics follow the platform's Kueue quota model (ClusterQueue/LocalQueue); no quota-side backend work is expected — the Dashboard reads quota through the Kubernetes API today.\n57\t- The metering data schema risk carried by the report computation work propagates here only through the report API contract, which is defined within this strategy.\n58\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b473b6dbc832cfdb","agent_id":"a4050c611fcde7715","session_id":"9043ac75-7a00-4a8d-a271-1ae0d81512e8","uuid":"40f9bf5d-b1b7-4269-972f-2ccf7e879e2e","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:24:14.476Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-933c1e990de5a8fd","permission_decision":{"decision