tion covers export integration for finance tooling, covering both CSV export and stable API retrieval against the documented report contract.\n47\t- The content is technically reviewed against the implemented reporting capability (computation, export, and Dashboard views) and reflects the behavior as built, including any metering-schema-driven caveats.\n48\t- Documentation includes worked examples of retrieving a report for a selectable time range via the export paths.\n49\t\n50\t## HLR Traceability\n51\t\n52\t- HLR-4 (P2): documentation covers report semantics (what counts as a GPU-hour) and export integration — fully covered by this epic.\n53\t\n54\t## Risks / Notes\n55\t\n56\t- The \"what counts as a GPU-hour\" definition originates in the GPU usage metering strategy's semantics; this epic documents it as landed, and is therefore sequenced after the reporting implementation.\n57\t- Owning team is not specified in the strategy; assigned to the team owning the report computation and export API (the primary documented surface) — confirm at planning.\n58\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b473b6dbc832cfdb","agent_id":"a4050c611fcde7715","session_id":"9043ac75-7a00-4a8d-a271-1ae0d81512e8","uuid":"1f874a13-6822-4f1e-89ee-6a4dbc0768dc","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:24:15.460Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-aac11b995eba4709","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9018 decomposition"}
