4\tNo circular dependencies. All three edges are justified by construction rules: E001→E002 is a Rule 13 artifact-consumer edge (Dashboard views build against the report API); E001→E003 and E002→E003 are Rule 11 docs-last edges. Frontmatter `dependencies` lists (E001: [], E002: [E001], E003: [E001, E002]) match the summary DAG diagram exactly, in the dependency→dependent convention. No konflux-onboarding, license-validation, or repo-onboarding epics exist, so Rules 7/8/10 parallelism is not implicated. The RHAISTRAT-9990 external dependency is properly kept out of the DAG (Rule 21, third party resolves) and gated via E001's acceptance criteria — the rule-compliant shape. Critical path length 3 fits the strategy size (M standard: 3-4). Cross-check of epic content found no uncaptured data/artifact dependencies: E002's Kueue quota read uses the existing Kubernetes API surface (no epic edge needed), and E003's content inputs are both edged.\n25\t\n26\t### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n27\tEach epic has a distinct component/team tuple (E001: Distributed Workloads/Distributed Workloads; E002: Dashboard/RHOAI Dashboard; E003: Documentation/Distributed Workloads), matching the owning teams in the architecture context files. No epic spans multiple components or teams. E001 is one logical change (one report-computation service with export output modes), not a heterogeneous monolith; E002 bundles two presentations of one administrator view surface — the compliant single-epic shape, not a duplication split. No scope duplication between E001 and E002 (backend surface vs. view surface, with a reconciliation AC tying them). Docs content authoring is correctly separated into E003 rather than mixed into the implementation epics. No epic exceeds the ~2-week guideline.\n28\t\n29\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n30\tNo Investigation epics — correctly so: the strategy's single open question (metering schema finalization) does not change which epics exist or their structure; the decomposition